#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:01.835--%3E00:00:03.420
msgid "Should I be looking at you?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:08.091--%3E00:00:11.220
msgid ""
"Okay. I hope you don't see\n"
"this, but it really helps to.."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:12.221--%3E00:00:13.222
msgid "In your opinion,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:13.972--%3E00:00:15.182
msgid "what is KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:17.601--%3E00:00:19.061
msgctxt "00:00:17.601-->00:00:19.061"
msgid "What is KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:21.146--%3E00:00:22.689
msgctxt "00:00:21.146-->00:00:22.689"
msgid "What is KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:25.609--%3E00:00:29.780
msgid ""
"It's a little bit hard\n"
"to explain how this really feels."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:29.863--%3E00:00:32.407
msgid ""
"It probably means something else\n"
"for different people, you know?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:32.491--%3E00:00:35.077
msgid ""
"In the early years,\n"
"it was a group of geeks coming together"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:35.160--%3E00:00:37.246
msgid ""
"and trying to hack some\n"
"cool stuff together."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:37.329--%3E00:00:40.791
msgid ""
"For Kalle and me and others,\n"
"it is nostalgia."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:40.874--%3E00:00:43.418
msgid ""
"Initially, it was the effort\n"
"of creating a desktop environment"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:43.502--%3E00:00:45.796
msgid "so that we will not be forced to use CDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:45.879--%3E00:00:50.467
msgid ""
"KDE started with Matthias Ettrich\n"
"sending this famous email saying,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:50.550--%3E00:00:53.220
msgid ""
"\"I want to create the Kool\n"
"Desktop Environment.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:53.303--%3E00:00:56.890
msgid ""
"For users, it's a software\n"
"environment that they are using."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:56.974--%3E00:00:57.683
msgid "But that's interesting"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:00:57.766--%3E00:01:01.436
msgid ""
"because an environment can\n"
"be more than just technology."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:01.520--%3E00:01:04.564
msgid ""
"KDE is this ambition\n"
"of changing the world."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:04.648--%3E00:01:10.445
msgid ""
"KDE is a community of like-minded people\n"
"who together work on maintaining a certain"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:10.529--%3E00:01:14.950
msgid ""
"kind of mindset towards how\n"
"software should be built."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:15.033--%3E00:01:19.746
msgid ""
"We don't spy on you. You get total control\n"
"of your hardware and your software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:19.830--%3E00:01:24.960
msgid ""
"KDE is freedom, really, and friendship.\n"
"KDE, to me, is the proof"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:25.043--%3E00:01:29.506
msgid ""
"that a lot of people with a lot\n"
"of goodwill can come together"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:29.590--%3E00:01:32.968
msgid ""
"and achieve something together.\n"
"While this sounds lofty,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:33.051--%3E00:01:36.805
msgid ""
"I think that part is more important\n"
"than the actual software being created."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:36.888--%3E00:01:40.017
msgid "Yeah, that's probably all of it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:40.892--%3E00:01:43.562
msgid "Well, how are we still around?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:01:47.190--%3E00:01:49.943
msgid "Yeah. That's a really good question."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:12.507--%3E00:02:18.972
msgid ""
"So in the mid-1990s, the internet was not\n"
"a common thing to have for people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:19.056--%3E00:02:23.435
msgid ""
"Even computers were not\n"
"necessarily in every household."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:23.518--%3E00:02:25.854
msgid ""
"The internet back\n"
"then was extremely nerdy,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:25.937--%3E00:02:29.691
msgid ""
"mostly people that had access\n"
"to it from university space."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:29.775--%3E00:02:34.571
msgid ""
"Companies started to have websites,\n"
"but I don't think they knew why."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:35.238--%3E00:02:39.951
msgid ""
"It was kind of academic. In the early 90s,\n"
"DOS was a dominant operating system,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:40.035--%3E00:02:43.330
msgid ""
"and it had almost every application\n"
"that you could think of."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:43.413--%3E00:02:47.501
msgid ""
"There were a couple of alternative\n"
"operating systems popping up."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:47.584--%3E00:02:51.046
msgid ""
"Microsoft Windows was one of those,\n"
"and it was starting to get popularity."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:51.129--%3E00:02:56.343
msgid ""
"But it was an operating system that was\n"
"fairly unstable. It was not that good."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:02:56.426--%3E00:03:00.555
msgid ""
"Microsoft software at\n"
"that time was really, really bad."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:00.639--%3E00:03:04.267
msgid ""
"I mean it was normal that a computer\n"
"when you were just typing a letter"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:04.351--%3E00:03:09.815
msgid ""
"or some work would regularly crash and\n"
"you would lose data if you don't hit save"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:09.898--%3E00:03:14.486
msgid ""
"and you had to reboot the machine.\n"
"You couldn't run two programs in parallel."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:14.569--%3E00:03:18.782
msgid ""
"Everybody thought that was normal.\n"
"It's a computer, it crashes."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:33.380--%3E00:03:37.467
msgid ""
"When Linux actually got initially\n"
"released, it was called Freax"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:37.551--%3E00:03:44.099
msgid ""
"and I immediately was fond of it and did\n"
"a download and joined the discussions."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:44.182--%3E00:03:47.060
msgid ""
"When this operating system\n"
"Linux came into the stage,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:47.144--%3E00:03:52.441
msgid ""
"it had some capabilities that neither DOS\n"
"or Windows at the time really supported."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:52.524--%3E00:03:54.943
msgid ""
"And one of them was multitasking.\n"
"So for the first time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:55.026--%3E00:03:58.447
msgid ""
"you had real multitasking\n"
"on consumer computers for free."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:03:58.530--%3E00:04:00.657
msgid ""
"This architecture gave\n"
"you a level of safety"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:00.740--%3E00:04:04.369
msgid ""
"that prevented one bad program\n"
"from crashing your system."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:04.453--%3E00:04:09.791
msgid ""
"So when Linus Torvalds releases this Linux\n"
"operating system, there's such a flurry"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:09.875--%3E00:04:13.378
msgid ""
"of excitement in the communities\n"
"to build something around Linux."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:13.462--%3E00:04:18.758
msgid ""
"Linux grew from one user to 10 in its\n"
"first year, then a few hundred."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:18.842--%3E00:04:22.512
msgid ""
"Linux was only really a couple\n"
"of years old at that time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:22.596--%3E00:04:28.101
msgid ""
"but had already made a reputation\n"
"for itself to be stable and cheap to run."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:29.436--%3E00:04:31.646
msgid "And then 1995 comes"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:34.316--%3E00:04:39.112
msgid ""
"and Microsoft launches a major upgrade to\n"
"their operating system called Windows 95."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:40.989--%3E00:04:44.367
msgid ""
"Windows 95 still wasn't\n"
"fully multitasking."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:44.451--%3E00:04:48.246
msgid ""
"Windows 95 still didn't solve\n"
"all the hangs and crashes,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:48.330--%3E00:04:52.834
msgid ""
"but the user experience\n"
"was fantastic for the era."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:52.918--%3E00:04:57.756
msgid ""
"And it opened the doors to make computers\n"
"really accessible to a large swath"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:04:57.839--%3E00:05:01.384
msgid ""
"of the population that before would\n"
"not have even considered using it or,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:01.468--%3E00:05:05.180
msgid ""
"you know, felt frustrated using it.\n"
"So for the first time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:05.263--%3E00:05:10.519
msgid ""
"they had a consumer operating system\n"
"available on mainstream computers"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:10.602--%3E00:05:11.937
msgid "that people could afford."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:12.020--%3E00:05:18.527
msgid ""
"Windows 95 is so easy,\n"
"even a talk show host can figure it out."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:18.610--%3E00:05:20.654
msgid "That took the world by storm."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:22.280--%3E00:05:27.077
msgid ""
"Linux on a desktop felt inferior.\n"
"It was really complicated."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:27.160--%3E00:05:30.747
msgid ""
"And to do a setup of your desktop\n"
"so that somehow you could work with,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:30.830--%3E00:05:34.751
msgid ""
"it took days of fiddling around\n"
"with configuration files,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:34.834--%3E00:05:38.547
msgid ""
"with weird syntaxes,\n"
"and bad or no documentation."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:38.630--%3E00:05:42.842
msgid ""
"Using Linux on the desktop was tedious.\n"
"Let's put it this way."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:42.926--%3E00:05:46.721
msgid ""
"I've been using Windows a little bit,\n"
"never liked it too much,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:46.805--%3E00:05:50.850
msgid ""
"but a lot of things could be done\n"
"graphically. And it was a lot easier,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:50.934--%3E00:05:54.729
msgid ""
"a lot more accessible,\n"
"especially also to less technical people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:54.813--%3E00:05:59.901
msgid ""
"Linux was very hard in that respect. You\n"
"know, you had a very steep learning curve."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:05:59.985--%3E00:06:02.904
msgid ""
"Most of us actually\n"
"worked in terminal windows"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:02.988--%3E00:06:07.659
msgid ""
"or if they had a graphical interface,\n"
"it was something like the XEmacs."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:07.742--%3E00:06:13.039
msgid ""
"Nobody ran Linux on the desktop except\n"
"a few couple of nerds with a huge pain"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:13.123--%3E00:06:17.127
msgid ""
"threshold. That was the sad\n"
"state of Linux on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:17.210--%3E00:06:20.964
msgid ""
"Linux is not only plexible in its\n"
"basic form, it's also free."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:21.047--%3E00:06:24.843
msgid ""
"You started seeing that it actually\n"
"was being used more and more,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:24.926--%3E00:06:27.220
msgid "especially by researchers, by students."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:27.304--%3E00:06:31.433
msgid ""
"And I think that's where a lot of it\n"
"started, down in the universities."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:38.315--%3E00:06:43.778
msgid ""
"In 1996, I was studying computer\n"
"science at the University of Tübingen."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:44.321--%3E00:06:46.656
msgid ""
"Constantly you were\n"
"asked by fellow students,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:46.740--%3E00:06:51.036
msgid ""
"I lost all my data, I lost all\n"
"my writings, the computer crashed,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:51.119--%3E00:06:53.121
msgid ""
"everything was awful.\n"
"Can you please help us?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:53.204--%3E00:06:56.750
msgid ""
"You study computer science, so obviously\n"
"you must know how to deal with that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:06:56.833--%3E00:07:00.378
msgid ""
"And I asked them, so why don't\n"
"you use a computer system that works?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:00.462--%3E00:07:03.340
msgid ""
"And the answer was always like,\n"
"I need Microsoft Word,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:03.423--%3E00:07:05.634
msgid "how else should I write my thesis?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:05.717--%3E00:07:10.972
msgid ""
"Okay, just write a word processor,\n"
"how hard can it be to fix that problem?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:12.390--%3E00:07:13.183
msgid "But of course,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:13.266--%3E00:07:17.812
msgid ""
"it didn't fix the problem because there\n"
"were still a lot of barriers to entry."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:17.896--%3E00:07:21.191
msgid ""
"I know a number of Windows users\n"
"who, they hate the system."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:21.274--%3E00:07:26.196
msgid ""
"They curse how it crashes, that you have\n"
"to save every time before you print."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:26.279--%3E00:07:30.784
msgid ""
"They're still happy because they're used\n"
"to it. The terminal was a scary thing"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:30.867--%3E00:07:35.455
msgid ""
"and everything had to be point and click\n"
"and mouse. That was the requirement."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:35.538--%3E00:07:37.123
msgid "If you wanted to write your homework,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:37.207--%3E00:07:41.294
msgid ""
"you were probably better off with Windows\n"
"than you were with Linux at the time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:41.378--%3E00:07:43.630
msgid "It was really not for home households."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:43.713--%3E00:07:48.426
msgid ""
"So to me, it was clear that Linux\n"
"as a system, or Unix in general,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:48.510--%3E00:07:53.348
msgid ""
"needed a friendly, nice environment\n"
"to be successful. That was the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:55.183--%3E00:07:58.728
msgid ""
"I founded the Linux\n"
"user group of Tübingen."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:07:58.812--%3E00:08:03.066
msgid ""
"This is also where at\n"
"one point I met Matthias."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:04.234--%3E00:08:09.906
msgid ""
"There was a consortium approach\n"
"to a UI from the open group called CDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:09.990--%3E00:08:12.492
msgid ""
"They called it the Common\n"
"Desktop Environment"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:12.575--%3E00:08:15.495
msgid ""
"which was a nightmare\n"
"designed by committee."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:15.578--%3E00:08:20.083
msgid ""
"We both independently had\n"
"a glimpse at the upcoming CDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:21.543--%3E00:08:27.006
msgid ""
"We were very disappointed and actually\n"
"afraid of this becoming the new standard,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:27.090--%3E00:08:28.299
msgid "because it was announced by Red Hat"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:28.383--%3E00:08:31.052
msgid ""
"that this is going to be\n"
"the standard for the Linux desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:31.136--%3E00:08:34.180
msgid "Then in 1996, on the 14th of October,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:34.264--%3E00:08:37.308
msgid ""
"we met on the campus at\n"
"Morgenstelle Tübingen,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:37.392--%3E00:08:40.186
msgid ""
"and then we came to the conclusion\n"
"that we have to do something."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:40.270--%3E00:08:43.106
msgid "We want to define the Linux desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:43.982--%3E00:08:47.861
msgid "KDE started as an attempt to bring Linux"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:47.944--%3E00:08:52.741
msgid ""
"or Unix to the masses as a user-friendly\n"
"system that everybody can use."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:08:57.036--%3E00:08:59.622
msgid ""
"They changed it.\n"
"It's not the same anymore."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:03.042--%3E00:09:06.046
msgid ""
"It was around here,\n"
"but it was a different setup."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:06.129--%3E00:09:09.090
msgid "No round tables, but rectangular tables."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:09.632--%3E00:09:10.884
msgid "This is actually the place"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:10.967--%3E00:09:16.848
msgid ""
"where we initially came up with the idea\n"
"of founding the KDE project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:16.931--%3E00:09:19.559
msgid "I think the vibes are still the same."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:19.642--%3E00:09:26.483
msgid ""
"Young people having ambitious ideas\n"
"and with a bright future,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:26.566--%3E00:09:31.821
msgid ""
"hopefully. People don't realize what\n"
"an incredible amount of resources it takes"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:31.905--%3E00:09:34.407
msgid "to make just about any software project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:34.491--%3E00:09:38.078
msgid ""
"You need many programmers\n"
"even to just do one program,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:38.161--%3E00:09:42.832
msgid ""
"much less create a complete system.\n"
"At the time, did it seem feasible"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:42.916--%3E00:09:46.377
msgid ""
"or crazy fantasy to even\n"
"attempt something like this?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:46.461--%3E00:09:49.756
msgid ""
"I was convinced from the very beginning\n"
"that this is feasible."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:49.839--%3E00:09:54.135
msgid ""
"You must be a little bit crazy,\n"
"you must be a little bit arrogant,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:54.219--%3E00:09:56.262
msgid "otherwise you will never start."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:09:56.346--%3E00:10:00.266
msgid ""
"What I had rather early in my mind\n"
"was a set of utilities and tools"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:00.350--%3E00:10:03.728
msgid ""
"that would be required to have\n"
"a nice desktop experience."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:05.730--%3E00:10:08.149
msgid "The problem was that it was really,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:08.233--%3E00:10:13.613
msgid ""
"really hard to develop a graphical\n"
"application for that system,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:13.696--%3E00:10:15.532
msgid "because nothing was standardized."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:15.615--%3E00:10:19.410
msgid ""
"Then Matthias mentioned that there's\n"
"this new library he just discovered,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:19.494--%3E00:10:24.916
msgid ""
"and it just works like we always thought\n"
"that it should work. When I discovered Qt,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:24.999--%3E00:10:29.295
msgid ""
"I think we called it Qt (\"QT\") before we met\n"
"the trolls who called it Qt (\"Cute\"), it felt like,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:29.379--%3E00:10:31.464
msgid "yes, that is the missing puzzle piece."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:31.548--%3E00:10:36.136
msgid ""
"That is a system that made it possible\n"
"to implement graphical applications"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:36.219--%3E00:10:41.182
msgid ""
"so much faster in higher quality than any\n"
"of the stuff I've seen before on Linux."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:41.266--%3E00:10:44.144
msgid ""
"It just felt like if we can\n"
"make this with a small team,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:44.227--%3E00:10:46.938
msgid ""
"then we need to have\n"
"a power tool like this."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:47.021--%3E00:10:50.567
msgid ""
"And then you wrote this?\n"
"Then I wrote that announcement."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:55.029--%3E00:10:58.283
msgid ""
"New project.\n"
"Kool Desktop Environment, KDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:10:58.783--%3E00:11:03.246
msgid ""
"Unix popularity grows thanks\n"
"to the free variants, mostly Linux."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:03.329--%3E00:11:07.542
msgid ""
"But still a consistent, nice looking,\n"
"free desktop environment is missing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:07.625--%3E00:11:11.254
msgid ""
"The idea is to create\n"
"a GUI for an end user."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:11.337--%3E00:11:13.256
msgid ""
"Somebody who wants to browse\n"
"the web with Linux,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:13.339--%3E00:11:15.675
msgid ""
"write some letters\n"
"and play some nice games."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:15.758--%3E00:11:20.722
msgid ""
"I don't have the time to do this all\n"
"alone, also since LyX is my main project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:20.805--%3E00:11:27.061
msgid ""
"But a thing like a desktop environment\n"
"can easily be cut into lots of parts."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:27.145--%3E00:11:31.816
msgid ""
"There is probably a part for you.\n"
"If you want to learn some X programming,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:31.900--%3E00:11:35.612
msgid ""
"why not do a small, neat project\n"
"for the K Desktop Environment?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:35.695--%3E00:11:38.948
msgid ""
"The stuff will be distributed\n"
"under the terms of the GPL."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:39.032--%3E00:11:42.660
msgid ""
"I admit the whole thing\n"
"sounds a bit like fantasy,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:42.744--%3E00:11:45.622
msgid "but it's very serious from my side."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:45.705--%3E00:11:49.626
msgid ""
"Everybody I'm talking to in the net world\n"
"would love a somewhat cleaner desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:49.709--%3E00:11:52.587
msgid "Qt is the chance to realize this."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:52.670--%3E00:11:57.342
msgid ""
"So let us join our rare\n"
"spare time and just do it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:11:57.543--%3E00:11:59.263
msgid "Regards."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:00.897--%3E00:12:03.723
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah. I remember.\n"
"I really struggled with English."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:03.806--%3E00:12:09.520
msgid ""
"Yeah, it brings back memories, and I\n"
"was thinking about where he was correct"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:09.604--%3E00:12:12.857
msgid ""
"and where he\n"
"was underestimating the efforts."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:12.941--%3E00:12:18.363
msgid ""
"I remember that it didn't take long\n"
"And I got a couple of responses."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:18.446--%3E00:12:21.199
msgid ""
"And one of the responses\n"
"I got was from Kalle."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:26.454--%3E00:12:29.624
msgid ""
"I didn't know Matthias\n"
"in person at that time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:29.707--%3E00:12:33.962
msgid "but I knew him through his software LyX,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:34.045--%3E00:12:36.547
msgid ""
"which I had used to write\n"
"my master's thesis in."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:36.631--%3E00:12:38.424
msgid ""
"So clearly this guy\n"
"knew what he was talking"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:38.508--%3E00:12:41.469
msgid ""
"about because he had already\n"
"written this substantial package,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:41.552--%3E00:12:46.849
msgid ""
"which was user-friendliness driven.\n"
"That was resonating a lot."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:46.933--%3E00:12:51.270
msgid ""
"I answered that post and said,\n"
"I might be in. This sounds interesting."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:51.980--%3E00:12:55.316
msgid ""
"Yeah, so we just started\n"
"discussing what do we need"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:55.400--%3E00:12:57.360
msgid "and then we started writing code."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:12:59.570--%3E00:13:03.574
msgid ""
"I was very confident that this is going\n"
"to be big and we had to be fast"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:03.658--%3E00:13:06.452
msgid ""
"because the race with CDE\n"
"was already going on."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:06.536--%3E00:13:09.080
msgid "So I had to start the infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:09.163--%3E00:13:12.166
msgid ""
"If you make a project like this,\n"
"you need a lot of different people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:12.250--%3E00:13:14.502
msgid ""
"You need people\n"
"that go out and promote it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:14.585--%3E00:13:17.630
msgid ""
"You need people who love\n"
"to write code, but..."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:17.714--%3E00:13:19.340
msgid "First and foremost, at the beginning,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:19.424--%3E00:13:21.342
msgid ""
"you need people\n"
"who provide the infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:21.426--%3E00:13:23.302
msgid ""
"There was no GitHub\n"
"like today or whatever."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:23.386--%3E00:13:26.723
msgid ""
"There was no infrastructure\n"
"in the internet we could reuse."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:26.806--%3E00:13:31.227
msgid ""
"So he was able to commandeer\n"
"some university resources for us."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:31.310--%3E00:13:34.105
msgid "That was the infamous FiWi02 machine,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:34.188--%3E00:13:37.859
msgid ""
"which technically was the print\n"
"server for the economics department,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:37.942--%3E00:13:44.449
msgid ""
"where I had a job. For the longest time,\n"
"we had FiWi02 in our email addresses."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:44.532--%3E00:13:46.451
msgid "Everybody really shared the same vision"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:46.534--%3E00:13:52.081
msgid ""
"and they contributed with what they knew\n"
"best. The first thing I wrote was KConfig,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:52.165--%3E00:13:56.669
msgid ""
"a class that stored configuration,\n"
"because one of the ex-commandments of KDE"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:56.753--%3E00:13:59.297
msgid ""
"was everything should be\n"
"configurable for the user."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:13:59.380--%3E00:14:04.594
msgid ""
"After a short time, like some weeks,\n"
"we already had stuff running,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:04.677--%3E00:14:10.725
msgid ""
"which was in some aspects more modern\n"
"looking than what was available"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:10.808--%3E00:14:16.314
msgid ""
"from any application on the Linux\n"
"desktop, on the X11 desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:16.397--%3E00:14:21.319
msgid ""
"So it took off very fast and we gained\n"
"a lot of developers and attention."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:21.402--%3E00:14:25.782
msgid ""
"That was mainly due to the Qt\n"
"library from Qt, from Trolltech."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:30.661--%3E00:14:32.455
msgid "You're running now the camera?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:32.538--%3E00:14:37.376
msgid ""
"Okay. The main reason\n"
"we really started Trolltech"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:37.460--%3E00:14:42.298
msgid ""
"was because we wanted to make life\n"
"easier for programmers like ourselves."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:42.382--%3E00:14:45.176
msgid ""
"Because we saw how frustrating\n"
"it was to use all these tools"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:45.259--%3E00:14:48.304
msgid ""
"that weren't good enough,\n"
"that didn't have good enough interfaces."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:48.388--%3E00:14:53.184
msgid ""
"The predominant graphics library\n"
"for Unix systems was X11 at that time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:53.267--%3E00:14:57.313
msgid ""
"That was limited to draw a pixel here,\n"
"draw a line here, draw a circle here."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:14:57.396--%3E00:15:00.316
msgid ""
"And then there were a couple\n"
"of building blocks on top of that,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:00.400--%3E00:15:01.901
msgid "of which Motif was one."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:03.361--%3E00:15:05.571
msgid "These all had a lot of problems."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:05.655--%3E00:15:09.534
msgid ""
"Back then, if you wanted to make\n"
"an X11 Hello World program,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:09.617--%3E00:15:14.747
msgid ""
"it was over 100 lines. They were no fun\n"
"to develop with, and Qt changed that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:14.831--%3E00:15:18.960
msgid ""
"First time I saw him, he was sitting\n"
"like this in front of his computer."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:19.043--%3E00:15:23.506
msgid ""
"And I took one short look at\n"
"the screen and I said, hey,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:23.589--%3E00:15:28.386
msgid ""
"I see you have Turbo Pascal 4.0 also.\n"
"And we were instant friends."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:28.469--%3E00:15:31.806
msgid ""
"Sort of love at first sight,\n"
"you know, among geeks."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:31.889--%3E00:15:37.186
msgid ""
"We, under the hood, tried to solve all\n"
"the difficult generic programming tasks"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:37.270--%3E00:15:41.816
msgid ""
"so that our customers in the open source\n"
"community could focus on what made"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:41.899--%3E00:15:43.943
msgid ""
"the software different\n"
"from all other software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:44.026--%3E00:15:49.699
msgid ""
"What makes Qt different is that it\n"
"was designed as a cross-platform toolkit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:49.782--%3E00:15:53.661
msgid ""
"Because of that, they were pushed quite\n"
"a bit because they needed to create"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:53.744--%3E00:15:58.332
msgid ""
"a toolkit that could actually\n"
"compete feature-wise with Windows 95."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:15:58.416--%3E00:16:02.879
msgid ""
"And that was far ahead than\n"
"anything that existed on Unix."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:04.213--%3E00:16:09.010
msgid ""
"It was very important for us to get free\n"
"software developers to use the toolkit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:09.093--%3E00:16:13.639
msgid ""
"And back then, the big thing was Usenet\n"
"groups where discussions were going on,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:13.723--%3E00:16:17.643
msgid ""
"new products were presented. So that\n"
"was in many ways our marketing channel."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:17.727--%3E00:16:20.688
msgid ""
"And that's how it reached,\n"
"eventually, Matthias Ettrich,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:20.771--%3E00:16:25.026
msgid ""
"and that's how he chose it to be\n"
"the basis of the KDE desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:26.444--%3E00:16:30.156
msgid ""
"Matthias' idea was, let's use Qt,\n"
"then we have a good building block"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:30.239--%3E00:16:35.995
msgid ""
"because it had so-called widgets, so push\n"
"button, slider, scroll bar, text entry."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:36.078--%3E00:16:40.291
msgid ""
"It was a game changer in terms of how\n"
"easy it was to develop things with it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:40.374--%3E00:16:45.546
msgid ""
"Now there was a drawback to it because Qt\n"
"was not really open source at that time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:46.088--%3E00:16:49.800
msgid ""
"Basically, our idea was, if you are\n"
"going to earn money using our software,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:49.884--%3E00:16:51.010
msgid "you're going to have to pay us."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:51.093--%3E00:16:55.806
msgid ""
"If you are doing this without\n"
"earning money, you don't have to pay."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:16:55.890--%3E00:17:00.478
msgid ""
"And that was the starting point of what\n"
"triggered those licensing discussions."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:08.194--%3E00:17:13.407
msgid ""
"I was working with the folks at Red\n"
"Hat on bringing Linux to the SPARC."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:13.491--%3E00:17:17.453
msgid ""
"And at some point, the news\n"
"of KDE gained enough momentum"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:17.536--%3E00:17:21.290
msgid ""
"that I took a look at it\n"
"and I was blown away."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:24.919--%3E00:17:29.548
msgid ""
"I remember emailing both Richard\n"
"Stallman at the Free Software Foundation"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:29.632--%3E00:17:32.885
msgid "and Erik Troan at Red Hat."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:32.969--%3E00:17:35.429
msgid ""
"Essentially, both of them\n"
"came back to me and they said,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:35.513--%3E00:17:41.477
msgid ""
"the problem is that the KDE desktop\n"
"is built on this foundation called Qt,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:41.560--%3E00:17:42.812
msgid "which is proprietary."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:42.895--%3E00:17:47.233
msgid ""
"The Free Software Foundation, especially\n"
"Richard Stallman, made a big fuss."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:49.610--%3E00:17:51.028
msgid "It's sad even today."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:51.112--%3E00:17:55.032
msgid ""
"There was a lot of political\n"
"infighting and a lot of ideology."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:55.116--%3E00:17:58.369
msgid ""
"There was one group around\n"
"the Free Software Foundation,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:17:58.452--%3E00:18:03.457
msgid ""
"which was started by Richard Stallman,\n"
"who was very extremist in his views."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:03.541--%3E00:18:09.088
msgid ""
"Distributing, developing proprietary\n"
"software is not a contribution to society."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:09.171--%3E00:18:11.882
msgid "It creates a social problem."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:11.966--%3E00:18:16.220
msgid ""
"And the aim of a free software\n"
"movement is to correct this problem."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:16.304--%3E00:18:18.639
msgid ""
"Free software,\n"
"originating from Richard Stallman,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:18.723--%3E00:18:21.767
msgid ""
"was very much focused\n"
"on the morality of it,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:21.851--%3E00:18:26.856
msgid ""
"that it's immoral to have\n"
"closed source software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:26.939--%3E00:18:30.484
msgid ""
"It means that the social system\n"
"of the program's distribution"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:30.568--%3E00:18:33.446
msgid "and use is unethical."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:33.529--%3E00:18:37.825
msgid ""
"Such software should not be developed\n"
"and it should not be used."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:37.908--%3E00:18:41.203
msgid ""
"And then there were other people\n"
"that included myself and Matthias"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:41.287--%3E00:18:45.333
msgid ""
"who were more pragmatic. For us it\n"
"was more open source software is good"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:45.416--%3E00:18:49.462
msgid ""
"because then many people can look at it\n"
"which means the software gets better."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:49.545--%3E00:18:52.798
msgid ""
"We thought this is actually\n"
"a good way to fund development"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:52.882--%3E00:18:56.719
msgid ""
"and make sure the framework actually\n"
"is competitive because everything"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:18:56.802--%3E00:19:01.724
msgid ""
"that we've seen so far otherwise in pure\n"
"open source technology was just not that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:01.807--%3E00:19:04.977
msgid ""
"I mean, it wasn't good enough.\n"
"The main argument was always,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:05.061--%3E00:19:10.900
msgid ""
"what if Trolltech becomes evil\n"
"or what if Microsoft buys them?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:11.692--%3E00:19:16.614
msgid ""
"The Trolltech people, and I pity them for\n"
"it, they also got under fire, of course."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:16.697--%3E00:19:22.203
msgid ""
"We were the big, bad capitalist company\n"
"wanting to control one of the major"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:22.286--%3E00:19:26.832
msgid ""
"development tools on Linux.\n"
"And that was so strange for us, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:26.916--%3E00:19:31.170
msgid ""
"sitting in Oslo, small office,\n"
"just a few geeks working together."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:32.338--%3E00:19:33.881
msgid "We got a lot of heat."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:33.964--%3E00:19:37.259
msgid ""
"Some people, especially in the US,\n"
"they really went mad."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:39.720--%3E00:19:42.014
msgid ""
"I didn't know they were\n"
"that tiny at the time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:42.098--%3E00:19:46.310
msgid ""
"They certainly looked like a serious\n"
"company. It was really high quality work."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:46.394--%3E00:19:49.188
msgid ""
"Couldn't be two guys,\n"
"or they were very good."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:49.271--%3E00:19:52.316
msgid ""
"I mean, as it turns out,\n"
"they were really exceptional developers."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:52.400--%3E00:19:57.113
msgid ""
"We were geeks, programmers.\n"
"We knew nothing about business."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:19:57.196--%3E00:20:01.534
msgid ""
"We knew nothing about sales.\n"
"We knew nothing about running a company."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:01.617--%3E00:20:04.829
msgid ""
"The two founders basically\n"
"lived off their wives' salaries"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:04.912--%3E00:20:08.207
msgid ""
"while they were starting to get\n"
"the company off the ground."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:08.290--%3E00:20:10.835
msgid ""
"So it was a little bit different\n"
"from a typical US-based"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:10.918--%3E00:20:13.712
msgid "venture capital-funded company."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:13.796--%3E00:20:20.302
msgid ""
"And then Red Hat, rather than just buying\n"
"Trolltech or making a deal with them,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:20.386--%3E00:20:22.847
msgid "created a counter project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:27.476--%3E00:20:34.150
msgid ""
"We essentially decided that what we could\n"
"do, recreate what the KDE folks had done,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:34.233--%3E00:20:38.487
msgid ""
"but instead of using Qt and C++, which\n"
"was the foundation for this other thing,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:38.571--%3E00:20:41.240
msgid ""
"we were going to use GTK to make sure\n"
"that it's in a foundation"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:41.323--%3E00:20:45.077
msgid ""
"that is free for everyone. It would meet\n"
"the business needs of people like Red Hat"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:45.161--%3E00:20:49.039
msgid ""
"and also the principal needs\n"
"of the Free Software Foundation."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:49.123--%3E00:20:51.750
msgid ""
"And that is how the GNOME\n"
"Project was born."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:20:56.714--%3E00:21:01.093
msgid ""
"We were surprised by it and we thought,\n"
"what will be the impact?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:01.177--%3E00:21:02.720
msgid "Will we have a big schism?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:03.762--%3E00:21:05.556
msgid "I can understand the reasoning,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:05.639--%3E00:21:10.436
msgid ""
"but I cannot understand why nobody\n"
"talked to us or to Trolltech."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:13.147--%3E00:21:16.150
msgid ""
"Then there was a lot\n"
"of writing done by journalists,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:16.233--%3E00:21:20.780
msgid ""
"by general holders of much opinion,\n"
"but writers of little code."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:20.863--%3E00:21:24.200
msgid ""
"People were talking past\n"
"each other and it got heated."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:25.367--%3E00:21:30.456
msgid ""
"A lot of it boiled down to Qt is evil,\n"
"KDE is evil, GNOME is good,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:30.539--%3E00:21:32.792
msgid "without people really knowing the details."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:32.875--%3E00:21:36.962
msgid ""
"I think that at the time it was felt\n"
"a lot more than it is today."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:37.046--%3E00:21:39.757
msgid ""
"Like today,\n"
"it's very common to see one project"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:39.840--%3E00:21:42.426
msgid ""
"and then 20 competitors\n"
"for the exact same thing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:42.510--%3E00:21:49.141
msgid ""
"But at the time, given how early we were,\n"
"how difficult it was to bootstrap,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:49.225--%3E00:21:54.230
msgid ""
"and just our size,\n"
"it did feel like a monumental split."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:54.313--%3E00:21:56.899
msgid "Then it was kind of a competition."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:21:56.982--%3E00:22:00.778
msgid ""
"Oh, they have that, and now we have\n"
"to do it, and we need to be better."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:00.861--%3E00:22:07.076
msgid ""
"I think, in a way, this whole\n"
"competition thing inspired both desktops."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:07.159--%3E00:22:09.411
msgid "I was sort of ambivalent around GNOME."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:09.495--%3E00:22:12.206
msgid ""
"It's always good if you have\n"
"a little bit of competition."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:12.289--%3E00:22:13.123
msgid "At the same time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:13.207--%3E00:22:17.169
msgid ""
"we were seeing that this was also\n"
"fragmenting the desktop story for Linux."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:17.253--%3E00:22:19.713
msgid ""
"That was something\n"
"I was thinking about quite a bit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:19.797--%3E00:22:25.052
msgid ""
"Did that competition help or not? And back\n"
"then I kind of tried to argue for myself:"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:25.135--%3E00:22:27.805
msgid ""
"yes, it did, because otherwise\n"
"it would have been too painful."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:27.888--%3E00:22:31.392
msgid ""
"But no, it didn't,\n"
"because the real competition,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:31.475--%3E00:22:33.561
msgid "Microsoft, was advancing fast."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:33.644--%3E00:22:40.192
msgid ""
"No, I think if we had worked together\n"
"against the commercial big world,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:40.276--%3E00:22:43.153
msgid ""
"it would have been much better.\n"
"At the same time, I mean,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:43.237--%3E00:22:44.488
msgid "you know, this is open source."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:44.572--%3E00:22:49.034
msgid ""
"Everybody's free to do whatever they want,\n"
"and you can't steer it, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:22:54.582--%3E00:23:00.629
msgid ""
"We spoke with Trolltech, and we knew\n"
"that they were on the same page."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:00.713--%3E00:23:03.465
msgid ""
"We need to find something\n"
"that works for free software,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:03.549--%3E00:23:07.094
msgid ""
"but also for them\n"
"so they can keep developing Qt."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:07.177--%3E00:23:11.599
msgid ""
"We knew that we wanted to support the free\n"
"software and open source community"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:11.682--%3E00:23:15.436
msgid ""
"and always make it available\n"
"for development of free software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:15.519--%3E00:23:18.147
msgid ""
"But we had to make sure\n"
"that we kept the control."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:18.230--%3E00:23:20.482
msgid "I mean, it wasn't just being paranoid."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:20.566--%3E00:23:23.986
msgid ""
"Richard Stallman, he really\n"
"wanted something to replace Qt."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:24.069--%3E00:23:30.868
msgid ""
"So they started the Harmony project, which\n"
"was a project to clone Qt under the GPL."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:30.951--%3E00:23:34.204
msgid ""
"And to us, that was a real threat,\n"
"because if they had succeeded,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:34.288--%3E00:23:37.916
msgid ""
"that could quickly have taken\n"
"over our place in the market,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:38.000--%3E00:23:41.587
msgid ""
"and it would have taken away all our\n"
"customers and all our open source users,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:41.670--%3E00:23:44.798
msgid ""
"and we would have to, you know,\n"
"do something else."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:47.343--%3E00:23:50.095
msgid "We had invested so much time and energy."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:23:55.684--%3E00:23:57.561
msgid "Still a bit emotional, you know."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:00.147--%3E00:24:01.148
msgid "Tough times,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:05.277--%3E00:24:09.573
msgid ""
"because it was our life work.\n"
"My recollection"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:09.657--%3E00:24:15.371
msgid ""
"is that this sort of forced\n"
"Trolltech to say, well,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:15.454--%3E00:24:18.457
msgid ""
"this can actually be\n"
"a threat to our business."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:18.540--%3E00:24:20.709
msgid "So is there something that we can do?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:22.670--%3E00:24:28.634
msgid ""
"We started communicating with some of the\n"
"KDE people. This was about the same time"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:28.717--%3E00:24:33.972
msgid ""
"that they were planning to have the first\n"
"developer meetup, the KDE One conference."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:34.056--%3E00:24:38.268
msgid ""
"We had at some point come to the\n"
"conclusion that it would be good"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:38.352--%3E00:24:42.064
msgid ""
"if at least the ones who were\n"
"involved most could meet in person."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:42.147--%3E00:24:45.401
msgid ""
"Yeah, so we started to pull this together.\n"
"I started making a budget"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:45.484--%3E00:24:49.530
msgid ""
"and I started to collect the sponsoring\n"
"that we had been offered."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:49.613--%3E00:24:51.490
msgid ""
"And this all went through\n"
"my private bank account"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:51.573--%3E00:24:54.660
msgid ""
"because there was no organization\n"
"to have a bank account."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:56.745--%3E00:24:58.622
msgid "We also asked the Trolltech people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:24:58.706--%3E00:25:04.211
msgid ""
"We got an email from Matthias Kalle\n"
"Dalheimer saying that they were planning"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:04.294--%3E00:25:10.092
msgid ""
"this and that they would very much like\n"
"someone from Trolltech to be there to,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:10.175--%3E00:25:13.303
msgid ""
"you know, continue some of these licensing\n"
"discussions face to face, and also,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:13.387--%3E00:25:16.849
msgid ""
"you know, developers speaking\n"
"to developers, giving each other feedback,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:16.932--%3E00:25:18.642
msgid "things they wanted in Qt."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:18.726--%3E00:25:24.481
msgid ""
"So we decided that Arnt and myself,\n"
"we would go down to the conference. And"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:26.191--%3E00:25:32.990
msgid ""
"then I booked with a Norwegian lawyer, and\n"
"I explained the whole situation to him."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:33.073--%3E00:25:36.869
msgid ""
"After a while, he looks at me\n"
"and he says, \"Are you telling me"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:36.952--%3E00:25:42.416
msgid ""
"that you want to pay me money so that you\n"
"can't stop giving something away for free?\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:42.499--%3E00:25:46.545
msgid "And I said, \"Yes, you have understood it.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:49.089--%3E00:25:55.429
msgid ""
"And then he told us, \"The only way to make\n"
"this 100% proof is to create an entity"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:25:55.512--%3E00:26:00.434
msgid ""
"separate from Trolltech that gets\n"
"the intellectual property rights to Qt,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:00.517--%3E00:26:02.311
msgid "in the sense that they can re-license it.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:02.394--%3E00:26:03.062
msgid "So in a way,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:03.145--%3E00:26:09.234
msgid ""
"the foundation already owns the code\n"
"for the Free Qt Edition and is entitled"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:09.318--%3E00:26:16.158
msgid ""
"in certain circumstances to relicense code\n"
"under a completely, totally free license."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:18.827--%3E00:26:23.582
msgid ""
"KDE One was the first physical\n"
"meeting of KDE developers."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:23.665--%3E00:26:27.002
msgid ""
"We only had names\n"
"and personalities coming from email."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:27.086--%3E00:26:29.546
msgid ""
"There were no pictures back\n"
"then on Usenet, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:29.630--%3E00:26:32.257
msgid ""
"You didn't know how people looked like.\n"
"There were no video calls."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:32.341--%3E00:26:34.259
msgid ""
"So, of course,\n"
"it was fun to meet each other."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:34.343--%3E00:26:39.681
msgid ""
"It was also amazing how well you knew\n"
"some people from just emails."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:39.765--%3E00:26:42.976
msgid ""
"It was incredible.\n"
"We understood each other immediately."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:43.060--%3E00:26:48.148
msgid ""
"We were immediately starting to setting\n"
"up our machines and starting working."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:48.232--%3E00:26:50.651
msgid "We prepared the very first KDE release,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:50.734--%3E00:26:53.779
msgid ""
"which got the code name Arnsberg\n"
"after the name of the town,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:53.862--%3E00:26:55.447
msgid "which they appreciated a lot."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:26:55.531--%3E00:27:00.035
msgid ""
"We also had some meetings and some people\n"
"showed what they have been working on."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:00.828--%3E00:27:04.832
msgid ""
"And this gave me the feeling, OK,\n"
"we are going to conquer the world."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:06.708--%3E00:27:08.544
msgid "The KDE guys, including me,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:08.627--%3E00:27:13.340
msgid ""
"were totally excited about writing\n"
"code together and doing stuff together."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:13.423--%3E00:27:17.344
msgid ""
"And the Trolltech people,\n"
"they already brought up like, we must talk"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:17.427--%3E00:27:22.015
msgid ""
"about this KDE Free Qt Foundation\n"
"thing to solve the licensing problem."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:22.099--%3E00:27:27.312
msgid ""
"I put forward what the lawyer\n"
"had said and the setup."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:27.396--%3E00:27:31.817
msgid ""
"But in order to be able to sign\n"
"that in any way, we needed a legal entity."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:31.900--%3E00:27:37.364
msgid ""
"And so we had to create the KDE e.V.,\n"
"eingetragener Verein."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:38.073--%3E00:27:41.326
msgid ""
"You know when you have two or three\n"
"Germans together they create a Verein"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:41.410--%3E00:27:45.956
msgid ""
"and so we had to do\n"
"that because of the licensing issue."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:46.039--%3E00:27:49.543
msgid ""
"So we agreed to do this and then\n"
"we started the whole process."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:50.043--%3E00:27:56.341
msgid ""
"We created the foundation in a way so that\n"
"the foundation is really very powerful"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:27:56.425--%3E00:28:00.304
msgid "and will survive any catastrophe."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:00.387--%3E00:28:06.310
msgid ""
"This was sort of in writing a way\n"
"of making sure that Qt remains available."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:06.393--%3E00:28:10.898
msgid ""
"It was really tough times, but\n"
"in hindsight, I think it made KDE better."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:10.981--%3E00:28:13.025
msgid "It made Qt better."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:13.108--%3E00:28:16.486
msgid ""
"And, you know, later on, Trolltech\n"
"was acquired by different entities"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:16.570--%3E00:28:21.158
msgid ""
"that could have changed the licensing. So\n"
"I think it really has served its purpose."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:21.241--%3E00:28:25.537
msgid ""
"I mean, still today, it's alive. It was a\n"
"very good thing that we got that in place"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:25.621--%3E00:28:29.374
msgid ""
"and it has ensured\n"
"that Qt has stayed free."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:35.297--%3E00:28:38.592
msgid ""
"At that point, I think the community\n"
"was still relatively small,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:38.675--%3E00:28:43.013
msgid ""
"because you had to be quite nerdy\n"
"in order to install it in the early days."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:43.096--%3E00:28:48.310
msgid ""
"KDE was lucky because of people like\n"
"Kalle who had contacts to print."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:49.436--%3E00:28:55.442
msgid ""
"One thing that drew a lot of people\n"
"was an article I wrote for c't magazine."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:55.525--%3E00:28:58.487
msgid ""
"It showed how to program\n"
"with KDE libraries"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:28:58.570--%3E00:29:02.157
msgid ""
"and how easy it is to create nice\n"
"programs on the Linux desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:02.240--%3E00:29:04.034
msgid "A lot of people joined after that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:04.117--%3E00:29:08.580
msgid ""
"So we got a lot of fresh new developers\n"
"who were eager in joining the band."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:09.289--%3E00:29:13.835
msgid ""
"It was still rather rudimentary at\n"
"that time, but it showed a lot of promise."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:13.919--%3E00:29:16.672
msgid ""
"A lot of the things we developed\n"
"came out of personal needs."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:16.755--%3E00:29:19.716
msgid ""
"I need something to manage\n"
"my appointments, and I thought, okay,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:19.800--%3E00:29:21.385
msgid "let's write a calendar application."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:21.468--%3E00:29:26.515
msgid ""
"Somebody needed a tea timer for measuring\n"
"how long they kept their tea bag."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:26.598--%3E00:29:28.934
msgid ""
"My own, you know,\n"
"sort of answering machine application."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:29.017--%3E00:29:31.603
msgid ""
"We needed to send emails,\n"
"so we wrote an email client."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:31.687--%3E00:29:34.481
msgid ""
"We needed to make drawings,\n"
"so we wrote a drawing program."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:34.564--%3E00:29:37.776
msgid ""
"We needed to write texts,\n"
"so we wrote a word processor."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:37.859--%3E00:29:40.112
msgid "The famous example is Torben Weis."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:40.195--%3E00:29:44.783
msgid ""
"He got assigned the task of writing the\n"
"KDE file manager, back then called KFM."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:44.866--%3E00:29:50.372
msgid ""
"What he actually did, he was writing\n"
"a complete, very functional web browser"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:50.455--%3E00:29:55.002
msgid ""
"who happens to have a file manager mode\n"
"so that it looks like a file manager."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:55.711--%3E00:29:58.714
msgid ""
"There was no direction\n"
"in terms of directing people"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:29:58.797--%3E00:30:01.508
msgid ""
"or somebody taking\n"
"decisions for the project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:01.591--%3E00:30:06.054
msgid ""
"We had one iron rule and that was whoever\n"
"does the work decides what gets done."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:06.138--%3E00:30:09.391
msgid ""
"We were not interested at all\n"
"in people with lots of opinion"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:09.474--%3E00:30:13.812
msgid ""
"but little willingness to do work.\n"
"It's writing software that counts."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:14.563--%3E00:30:16.231
msgid "A bit after KDE One,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:16.314--%3E00:30:20.610
msgid ""
"we would do the first beta and then\n"
"finishing the first release, KDE 1.0."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:21.653--%3E00:30:24.740
msgid ""
"The core components were around five,\n"
"six different things."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:24.823--%3E00:30:27.534
msgid ""
"There was a window manager,\n"
"which you needed on X11."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:27.617--%3E00:30:33.123
msgid ""
"There was a small panel at the bottom.\n"
"There was a small text editor, KEdit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:33.206--%3E00:30:37.461
msgid ""
"There was an email program, KMail.\n"
"All the names started with K."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:37.544--%3E00:30:41.840
msgid ""
"That was still an ongoing thing.\n"
"A small web browser which could do HTML3,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:41.923--%3E00:30:43.717
msgid ""
"which was sort of the standard at\n"
"that time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:43.800--%3E00:30:47.095
msgid ""
"and of course a terminal\n"
"to have that as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:49.097--%3E00:30:54.978
msgid ""
"The first version got a lot of attention.\n"
"Version 1.0 was already the best"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:55.062--%3E00:30:57.898
msgid ""
"environment you could\n"
"technically run on Linux."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:30:57.981--%3E00:31:01.485
msgid ""
"It was very functional.\n"
"It was pretty stable."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:04.362--%3E00:31:07.074
msgid ""
"The Linux distributions\n"
"started to include it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:07.157--%3E00:31:10.911
msgid ""
"It was the natural choice\n"
"in Germany to go with SUSE"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:10.994--%3E00:31:14.456
msgid "and KDE was first choice there."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:14.539--%3E00:31:17.751
msgid ""
"It was pre-selected.\n"
"That gave us a lot of feedback."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:17.834--%3E00:31:21.380
msgid ""
"That gave us a lot of users who were\n"
"just installing Linux from a distribution"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:21.463--%3E00:31:24.674
msgid ""
"and then got KDE automatically as\n"
"part of the installation process."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:24.758--%3E00:31:28.970
msgid ""
"And the feeling about Linux\n"
"and KDE was it's rising,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:29.054--%3E00:31:30.889
msgid "it's growing, it's a big thing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:36.394--%3E00:31:40.690
msgid ""
"As far as the growth goes... In the\n"
"beginning, I was tracking the downloads."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:40.774--%3E00:31:42.734
msgid ""
"I'm going to say exponentially\n"
"because I don't know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:42.818--%3E00:31:47.239
msgid ""
"which is another word of saying I don't\n"
"know. Exponential growth for years."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:47.322--%3E00:31:51.076
msgid ""
"We didn't care much because\n"
"if you don't look for investors,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:51.159--%3E00:31:53.370
msgid "what good is it to show a growth rate?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:54.079--%3E00:31:57.666
msgid ""
"The only growth we were really\n"
"interested in is developers."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:31:58.208--%3E00:32:01.711
msgid ""
"And it felt like there was a constant\n"
"supply of people actually joining"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:01.795--%3E00:32:04.047
msgid "and had new interesting projects."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:05.215--%3E00:32:09.970
msgid ""
"By far the biggest impact made\n"
"Konqueror, the KDE web browser."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:17.894--%3E00:32:23.400
msgid ""
"This started out around, I think, in 97 or\n"
"something like that with the old library"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:23.483--%3E00:32:28.530
msgid ""
"that we had before, KHTMLW,\n"
"which was able to render HTML3."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:28.613--%3E00:32:34.327
msgid ""
"At the same time, HTML4 came out\n"
"and Netscape added JavaScript support."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:34.411--%3E00:32:38.707
msgid ""
"Dynamic HTML is a very fundamental\n"
"difference from what you've seen before."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:38.790--%3E00:32:41.376
msgid ""
"You can build real applications\n"
"now on the internet."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:41.460--%3E00:32:45.005
msgid ""
"And we were seeing that our old browser\n"
"engine was completely falling apart."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:45.088--%3E00:32:47.632
msgid "Web became more and more important."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:47.716--%3E00:32:51.761
msgid ""
"And a desktop without an integrated\n"
"web browser is not quite working."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:51.845--%3E00:32:54.431
msgid ""
"We all agreed that we have\n"
"to do a complete rewrite."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:54.514--%3E00:32:57.058
msgid ""
"The old architecture\n"
"was just not extendable."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:32:57.142--%3E00:32:59.644
msgid "But nobody really felt like starting it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:01.396--%3E00:33:03.190
msgid "At some point, I got an idea."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:03.273--%3E00:33:07.194
msgid ""
"Can I actually write something\n"
"that generates me code for the whole spec?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:07.277--%3E00:33:11.406
msgid ""
"What was really amazing was that I could\n"
"hook it up mostly to the existing parser"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:11.490--%3E00:33:13.909
msgid "from the old KHTMLW project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:13.992--%3E00:33:17.996
msgid ""
"After two weeks or something like that, I\n"
"had some basic things rendering on screen."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:18.079--%3E00:33:22.167
msgid ""
"I was basically hooked at that point.\n"
"Yes, I can get something working."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:22.250--%3E00:33:24.044
msgid "But at that point in time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:24.127--%3E00:33:28.173
msgid ""
"Netscape was adding JavaScript support\n"
"and some scriptability to the engine."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:28.256--%3E00:33:33.094
msgid ""
"The browser would become exponentially\n"
"more complex all the time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:33.178--%3E00:33:37.557
msgid ""
"It was almost impossible. And yes, at\n"
"some point I thought, \"We cannot follow.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:37.641--%3E00:33:41.311
msgid ""
"The great thing about it was that there\n"
"was another guy out there, Harri Porten,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:41.394--%3E00:33:44.689
msgid ""
"who then at some point raised his voice\n"
"in the mailing list and said, \"Oh,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:44.773--%3E00:33:46.816
msgid ""
"I've developed a JavaScript\n"
"engine for fun."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:46.900--%3E00:33:48.818
msgid ""
"What about, you know,\n"
"hooking those things up?\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:48.902--%3E00:33:51.696
msgid ""
"And I said, \"Yeah, that sounds cool.\n"
"Let's do it.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:52.614--%3E00:33:55.867
msgid ""
"So that was when, I'd say, the modern\n"
"KHTML came really into existence."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:33:55.951--%3E00:34:01.164
msgid ""
"A little while later, the CSS2 spec\n"
"came out, completely changing, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:01.248--%3E00:34:03.416
msgid ""
"how things got rendered,\n"
"which basically meant"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:03.500--%3E00:34:08.046
msgid ""
"that we had to separate out the layouting\n"
"and rendering from the DOM representation."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:08.129--%3E00:34:12.300
msgid ""
"And that's what we did then at that time.\n"
"We did lots of architectural work there"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:12.384--%3E00:34:16.471
msgid ""
"in the beginnings of 2000 to get\n"
"these things working and up to speed."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:16.554--%3E00:34:17.806
msgid "That was a pretty big effort,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:17.889--%3E00:34:22.602
msgid ""
"but we got that far that we had actually\n"
"an engine that was absolutely competitive."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:22.686--%3E00:34:27.899
msgid ""
"It was in many ways better than what at\n"
"that time Mozilla had to offer."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:27.983--%3E00:34:33.029
msgid ""
"And in October 2000, KDE 2.0 came out\n"
"and that was the first KDE release where"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:33.113--%3E00:34:37.659
msgid ""
"we had a Konqueror web browser and where\n"
"we used KHTML as the rendering engine."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:37.742--%3E00:34:44.374
msgid ""
"The big advantage of KHTML was that it was\n"
"a very elegant design and it was a small,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:44.457--%3E00:34:49.170
msgid ""
"very focused engine.\n"
"That engineering challenge is crazy."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:49.254--%3E00:34:52.757
msgid ""
"I think we were like the smallest\n"
"web render team on the planet"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:52.841--%3E00:34:56.303
msgid ""
"and created something\n"
"so brilliant that's still in use today."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:56.386--%3E00:34:58.972
msgid "Got something totally new for you now."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:34:59.556--%3E00:35:05.478
msgid ""
"It's called Safari,\n"
"and it is a turbo browser for Mac OS X."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:06.438--%3E00:35:08.064
msgid "Apple actually went out and said"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:08.148--%3E00:35:12.861
msgid ""
"that they're picking up KHTML as\n"
"their basis for their Safari browser,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:14.112--%3E00:35:15.989
msgid "renaming it to WebKit later on,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:16.531--%3E00:35:19.576
msgid "and Chrome emerged from WebKit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:27.000--%3E00:35:28.877
msgid "Around the end of the 90s,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:28.960--%3E00:35:34.507
msgid ""
"KDE started to work on their second\n"
"revision of the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:34.591--%3E00:35:38.762
msgid ""
"2.0 was kind of intriguing because\n"
"they were trying new things and they were"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:38.845--%3E00:35:42.474
msgid ""
"introducing some new architectures\n"
"to the software that were pretty cool."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:42.557--%3E00:35:44.851
msgid "So I kind of had half an eye on it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:44.934--%3E00:35:49.439
msgid ""
"In 2000 at the time, I was running\n"
"a company and then the bubble burst,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:49.522--%3E00:35:52.525
msgid ""
"which meant our funding went away.\n"
"We wound the company down, unfortunately."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:52.609--%3E00:35:55.612
msgid ""
"I thought I'd take a few months off, and\n"
"it turns out I'm not really good at that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:55.695--%3E00:35:59.616
msgid ""
"So about a week later,\n"
"I looked at this KDE 2 thing again,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:35:59.699--%3E00:36:02.285
msgid ""
"and they had just released\n"
"one-point-something."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:02.369--%3E00:36:05.080
msgid ""
"I think it was codenamed Krash,\n"
"because it did, it crashed a lot."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:05.163--%3E00:36:06.164
msgid "Crash with a K, of course."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:06.247--%3E00:36:10.502
msgid ""
"So I built it on my machine at home\n"
"and noticed a small bug in it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:10.585--%3E00:36:16.383
msgid ""
"I had nothing else to do, so I wrote up a\n"
"small patch, sent it off and went to bed."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:16.966--%3E00:36:20.637
msgid ""
"And when I got up the next morning,\n"
"there was an email response saying,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:20.720--%3E00:36:24.391
msgid ""
"thank you very much for the patch.\n"
"It's been applied. And I was like, what?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:24.474--%3E00:36:29.104
msgid ""
"That's way too fast. I updated\n"
"my source code and there was my fix."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:29.187--%3E00:36:31.856
msgid "It was a little bit like a drug, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:31.940--%3E00:36:34.484
msgid ""
"this feedback and this community\n"
"of people that are building something"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:34.567--%3E00:36:38.530
msgid ""
"that was exciting and cool. And you could\n"
"just show up and be a part of it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:42.700--%3E00:36:47.288
msgid ""
"In 2000, I visited\n"
"Linux Expo in Frankfurt."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:47.831--%3E00:36:49.249
msgid "So I sat in the audience"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:49.332--%3E00:36:53.753
msgid ""
"when there was this big prize for the best\n"
"open source project, something like that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:53.837--%3E00:36:57.674
msgid ""
"So I was amazed sitting there in the\n"
"audience seeing Linus Torvalds giving"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:36:57.757--%3E00:37:03.263
msgid ""
"a prize to the KDE developers.\n"
"Later I went to the booth of KDE"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:03.346--%3E00:37:08.101
msgid ""
"and Linus was also there\n"
"and Martin was showing KDE to Linus."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:08.184--%3E00:37:11.813
msgid ""
"Martin later told me that this was one\n"
"of the most embarrassing moments for him"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:11.896--%3E00:37:15.442
msgid ""
"because KDE crashed when he\n"
"showed it to Linus Torvalds."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:15.525--%3E00:37:19.696
msgid ""
"That was the time when people\n"
"actually hacked at the booth"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:19.779--%3E00:37:21.823
msgid ""
"and people were coming\n"
"together to develop things."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:21.906--%3E00:37:24.742
msgid ""
"And somebody had compiled a new\n"
"version with some new features"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:24.826--%3E00:37:29.164
msgid ""
"and there was some bug somewhere. And this\n"
"was running on the demo computer there."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:29.247--%3E00:37:34.043
msgid ""
"I'm using KDE and KOffice tools.\n"
"That's actually a project"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:34.127--%3E00:37:38.965
msgid ""
"that a lot of people are working on\n"
"and that could make it come about."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:40.049--%3E00:37:42.844
msgid "And I think it will happen."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:42.927--%3E00:37:49.017
msgid ""
"I met him once and he recognized me\n"
"and said something friendly about KDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:49.893--%3E00:37:52.645
msgid ""
"He was already like greater\n"
"than life, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:52.729--%3E00:37:55.023
msgid "this mystical figure in the background."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:37:59.694--%3E00:38:05.617
msgid ""
"KDE 2.0 came out and it rapidly became stable.\n"
"Probably by 2.2, it was just rock solid."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:05.700--%3E00:38:07.994
msgid ""
"And that was in part\n"
"because Qt is a great library"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:08.077--%3E00:38:10.205
msgid ""
"and the developers working\n"
"on it put in a ton of effort."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:10.288--%3E00:38:15.418
msgid ""
"And then we knew that we needed testers,\n"
"we needed UI designers, graphics artists."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:15.502--%3E00:38:19.881
msgid ""
"We had new icons, very colorful.\n"
"Not all people liked that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:19.964--%3E00:38:25.929
msgid ""
"Torsten Rahn was doing them, and he\n"
"studied physics, and he implemented these"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:26.012--%3E00:38:32.185
msgid ""
"physical light effects in the icons\n"
"with only 16 times 16 pixels,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:32.268--%3E00:38:37.524
msgid ""
"and it was fascinating.\n"
"But it was a consistent look."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:37.607--%3E00:38:42.445
msgid ""
"If you look at KDE screenshots from\n"
"the early time now, they look very dated."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:42.529--%3E00:38:46.658
msgid ""
"But I found KDE beautiful back then\n"
"because it had a consistent look and feel."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:46.741--%3E00:38:51.120
msgid ""
"So you could really create\n"
"your workflows in the system"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:51.204--%3E00:38:53.998
msgid "and in Windows it was not possible at all."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:54.541--%3E00:38:58.711
msgid ""
"And that's when the majority\n"
"of users began moving to KDE, in part"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:38:58.795--%3E00:39:02.298
msgid ""
"because Linux was starting to grow and\n"
"people were moving away from old school"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:02.382--%3E00:39:06.761
msgid ""
"window managers to desktop environments\n"
"and KDE was kind of the choice."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:06.844--%3E00:39:10.598
msgid ""
"Of course, as things developed,\n"
"we were starting to get a bit ambitious"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:10.682--%3E00:39:13.643
msgid ""
"and we said, yes, I mean,\n"
"we want to compete with Windows."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:13.726--%3E00:39:17.063
msgid ""
"And I think some of the others probably\n"
"had that goal from the very beginning."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:17.146--%3E00:39:20.233
msgid ""
"It was very much for my purposes\n"
"a good competitor."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:20.316--%3E00:39:22.485
msgid "It felt very organized and systemized."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:22.569--%3E00:39:26.114
msgid ""
"It was sort of fun to see how far can\n"
"we actually push things, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:26.197--%3E00:39:30.660
msgid ""
"what can we achieve? Many people\n"
"thought that they were very close."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:31.202--%3E00:39:33.162
msgid "It became kind of this inside joke."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:33.246--%3E00:39:38.167
msgid ""
"We said, OK, next year will be the year\n"
"of the Linux desktop when we take over."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:38.251--%3E00:39:43.089
msgid ""
"Yeah, the goal of world domination\n"
"is always there, of course."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:49.679--%3E00:39:51.764
msgid "Then KDE 3 happened."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:51.848--%3E00:39:54.225
msgid "KDE's software was in a pretty good place."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:54.309--%3E00:39:58.271
msgid ""
"It was very stable,\n"
"very functional, very fast."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:39:58.354--%3E00:40:01.983
msgid ""
"We didn't want to spend time going back.\n"
"We didn't need to either go back"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:02.066--%3E00:40:05.653
msgid ""
"and rewrite the parts that were already\n"
"working. We needed more, not different."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:05.737--%3E00:40:09.490
msgid ""
"If you install KDE 2 and you install\n"
"KDE 3, they might look different,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:09.574--%3E00:40:12.285
msgid ""
"but just because we decided\n"
"to change the styling."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:12.368--%3E00:40:16.039
msgid ""
"KDE started of course with having\n"
"a desktop and all the sort of basic tools"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:16.122--%3E00:40:19.042
msgid ""
"that you would expect\n"
"to come along with that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:19.125--%3E00:40:23.963
msgid ""
"And then soon afterwards, it broadened\n"
"to also providing productivity software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:24.922--%3E00:40:28.676
msgid ""
"digiKam is one of my favorite\n"
"applications for managing photos."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:28.760--%3E00:40:32.096
msgid ""
"I once thought it would be\n"
"a good idea to buy Adobe software"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:32.180--%3E00:40:34.349
msgid "to see how real software works,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:34.432--%3E00:40:40.355
msgid ""
"and I was very frustrated and went back\n"
"to digiKam because it's just way better."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:40.980--%3E00:40:44.108
msgid "The applications that grew the fastest"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:44.192--%3E00:40:47.487
msgid ""
"and the widest were actually\n"
"the content creation ones."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:47.570--%3E00:40:52.158
msgid ""
"The Krita application was one of those.\n"
"As well as our video editor, Kdenlive."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:52.241--%3E00:40:55.954
msgid ""
"Later the Dolphin file manager.\n"
"The Amarok music player."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:56.037--%3E00:40:58.414
msgid ""
"There are many,\n"
"many more KDE applications."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:58.498--%3E00:40:59.707
msgid "I mean, we can, I don't know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:40:59.791--%3E00:41:03.753
msgid ""
"maybe we can do some graphics\n"
"or whatever with the universe of KDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:19.394--%3E00:41:23.272
msgid ""
"My talk is over there in that building,\n"
"so we can be at that door."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:32.323--%3E00:41:34.450
msgid "Hello. Are you from the organization?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:34.534--%3E00:41:38.287
msgid ""
"Yes. I'm the next person\n"
"giving a talk. Ah, okay."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:41.332--%3E00:41:42.750
msgid "Do you know what KDE is?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:43.376--%3E00:41:45.378
msgid "I'm a Mac user. You're a Mac user."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:46.170--%3E00:41:48.506
msgid ""
"Oh, no, you have made\n"
"all of us your enemy."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:48.589--%3E00:41:51.926
msgid "You should know. You should GNOME."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:53.261--%3E00:41:55.304
msgid "I don't know. A logo with a foot."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:41:56.889--%3E00:42:01.644
msgid ""
"I read somewhere that you're trying\n"
"to get rid of the logo with the foot?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:02.228--%3E00:42:07.024
msgid ""
"Why? Tried to get what?\n"
"The GNOME logo is a foot."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:07.108--%3E00:42:08.901
msgid ""
"Which makes so much sense,\n"
"you should keep it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:08.985--%3E00:42:11.195
msgid ""
"I mean, it makes zero sense,\n"
"but it's nice."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:11.279--%3E00:42:13.364
msgid ""
"Yeah, definitely. Okay,\n"
"I should go and prepare my talk."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:13.448--%3E00:42:14.449
msgid "See you later."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:28.504--%3E00:42:29.630
msgid "Is it very fancy?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:38.431--%3E00:42:41.058
msgid ""
"You know, it happens. When you release\n"
"a big version, things break."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:41.142--%3E00:42:46.647
msgid ""
"You do your best effort for things not\n"
"to break, but sometimes they do, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:46.731--%3E00:42:48.858
msgid "And it's what happened here, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:48.941--%3E00:42:52.028
msgid ""
"We released KDE 4,\n"
"and it was not a great success."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:52.111--%3E00:42:56.824
msgid ""
"There was one point where I lost nearly\n"
"faith that this is going to work out,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 7 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:42:56.908--%3E00:43:04.082
msgid ""
"and that was the KDE 4.x times.\n"
"We were quite close to not making it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:06.334--%3E00:43:11.297
msgid ""
"KDE 4 was a huge release.\n"
"KDE was very ambitious about it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:11.380--%3E00:43:15.968
msgid ""
"The main problem is we changed\n"
"too many things at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:16.052--%3E00:43:20.973
msgid ""
"Qt also had a major version step plan,\n"
"so they went to Qt 4,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:21.057--%3E00:43:26.562
msgid ""
"also changed a lot of things. And that\n"
"made it a very big step from Qt 3 to Qt 4."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:26.646--%3E00:43:31.234
msgid ""
"People had to bite the bullet and do\n"
"the porting work that was required."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:31.317--%3E00:43:36.322
msgid ""
"At the same time, the desktop components\n"
"had basically remained unchanged."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:36.405--%3E00:43:41.702
msgid ""
"We just built on them since 2.0. It\n"
"was getting harder and harder to maintain"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:41.786--%3E00:43:46.707
msgid ""
"because of earlier architectural decisions\n"
"and the evolving expectations of people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:46.791--%3E00:43:50.044
msgid ""
"We had done everything\n"
"we could do with the code base."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:50.128--%3E00:43:54.132
msgid ""
"And to get a step further,\n"
"to fix some of the more serious,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:54.215--%3E00:43:57.885
msgid ""
"more conceptual problems,\n"
"we would have to do a bigger step."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:43:57.969--%3E00:44:01.597
msgid ""
"And so I made the really hard decision,\n"
"we need to rewrite this bit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:01.681--%3E00:44:07.436
msgid ""
"He had a very specific vision about KDE\n"
"and what he thought KDE could become."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:07.520--%3E00:44:11.107
msgid ""
"I worked quietly on my own\n"
"for about almost a year."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:11.607--%3E00:44:12.733
msgid "Like, what would it look like?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:12.817--%3E00:44:14.193
msgid "What would it be?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:14.277--%3E00:44:19.031
msgid ""
"Is it realistic to do this? And so I kind\n"
"of sat down, I built some principles."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:19.115--%3E00:44:21.868
msgid ""
"Nothing should just appear and disappear.\n"
"Everything should move in and out."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:21.951--%3E00:44:24.745
msgid ""
"And this is a time when animation\n"
"was, like, not really a thing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:24.829--%3E00:44:27.748
msgid ""
"The system tray needs to be under\n"
"full control of the host application,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:27.832--%3E00:44:30.918
msgid ""
"the desktop, so we can\n"
"consistently style them,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:31.002--%3E00:44:33.004
msgid ""
"consistently provide\n"
"an interaction pattern for them"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:33.087--%3E00:44:34.881
msgid "and consistently make them accessible."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:34.964--%3E00:44:38.259
msgid ""
"That meant introducing new\n"
"technologies lower in the stack."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:38.342--%3E00:44:44.265
msgid ""
"But that rewrite from the ground up had\n"
"inherent risks. It's a huge code base"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 7 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:44.348--%3E00:44:51.647
msgid ""
"and we may have gone a little overboard in\n"
"the changes that we wanted to introduce."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:51.731--%3E00:44:57.361
msgid ""
"So this was really a big pile\n"
"of work and exhausting, I'd say."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:44:57.862--%3E00:45:00.615
msgid ""
"And we had been working\n"
"on it for a long time, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:00.698--%3E00:45:03.659
msgid ""
"If you see from KDE 3,\n"
"it's six years already."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:03.743--%3E00:45:08.456
msgid ""
"What we didn't realize, looking back\n"
"at it now, is that we had structured"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:08.539--%3E00:45:12.543
msgid ""
"our release process in the wrong\n"
"way for this kind of project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:12.627--%3E00:45:17.340
msgid ""
"And it took longer than the libraries\n"
"and longer than the applications in many"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:17.423--%3E00:45:21.552
msgid ""
"cases, in large part because\n"
"they weren't being rewritten."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:21.636--%3E00:45:25.640
msgid ""
"We also had lost some contributors\n"
"in the meantime who had helped start it"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:25.723--%3E00:45:29.226
msgid ""
"because perhaps they ran out\n"
"of patience not seeing it released."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:29.310--%3E00:45:33.064
msgid ""
"The number of people that were\n"
"contributing was in decline"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:33.147--%3E00:45:36.442
msgid ""
"and also the number\n"
"of users was in decline."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:36.525--%3E00:45:39.946
msgid ""
"Some of the people just went to use GNOME\n"
"or some other desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:40.029--%3E00:45:44.909
msgid ""
"The pressure to actually do a release\n"
"became huge. And it was probably one"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:44.992--%3E00:45:50.957
msgid ""
"of the more difficult decisions\n"
"to release KDE 4.0 as it was, not finished."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:51.040--%3E00:45:53.417
msgid "We decided to release the libraries,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:53.501--%3E00:45:57.254
msgid ""
"release essentially a preview of the\n"
"desktop, and then release the applications"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:45:57.338--%3E00:46:02.301
msgid ""
"that were ready. So we knew it was not\n"
"perfect, but it had huge potential."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:04.512--%3E00:46:08.474
msgid ""
"We did this release event in Mountain\n"
"View where we had a keynote"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:08.557--%3E00:46:14.772
msgid ""
"and we had live streaming and Aaron was\n"
"preparing it like a Steve Jobs keynote."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:14.855--%3E00:46:16.274
msgid "Today we take it for granted, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:16.357--%3E00:46:19.193
msgid ""
"You do a Twitch stream or whatever and\n"
"people are like chatting in the comments."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:19.276--%3E00:46:22.905
msgid ""
"This was very high-tech at the time,\n"
"right, and felt very futuristic."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:22.989--%3E00:46:27.994
msgid ""
"And then we have our new desktop shell,\n"
"Plasma, which unifies the panels,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:28.077--%3E00:46:30.413
msgid "the taskbars, with widgets on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:30.496--%3E00:46:32.999
msgid "That felt like something big was starting."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:35.042--%3E00:46:38.045
msgid ""
"Turned out a little bit\n"
"different than we expected."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:54.270--%3E00:46:58.357
msgid ""
"Our users at that time were\n"
"used to a very featureful,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:46:58.441--%3E00:47:01.068
msgid "very powerful, very polished system,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 7 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:01.152--%3E00:47:08.492
msgid ""
"and they were disappointed and couldn't\n"
"really see where we wanted to be going."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:08.576--%3E00:47:12.705
msgid ""
"Probably also a problem\n"
"of our lack of communication."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:12.788--%3E00:47:17.001
msgid ""
"We asked Linux distributions\n"
"not to ship that as the default,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:17.084--%3E00:47:22.465
msgid ""
"allow people to try it as a preview.\n"
"To their credit, most did that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:22.548--%3E00:47:23.966
msgid "And some didn't."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:24.967--%3E00:47:28.262
msgid ""
"A lot of users just\n"
"installed the next version,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:28.346--%3E00:47:31.807
msgid ""
"expected it to work as well as\n"
"all the other versions they tried,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:31.891--%3E00:47:36.771
msgid ""
"and it looked different, it worked\n"
"differently, and they were not satisfied."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:36.854--%3E00:47:41.942
msgid ""
"It was crashing, it was not stable. I\n"
"recompiled my desktop a few times a week."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:42.026--%3E00:47:46.989
msgid ""
"I several times lost my own work\n"
"because my desktop crashed"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:47.073--%3E00:47:48.032
msgid "and took everything with it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:48.115--%3E00:47:53.037
msgid ""
"And it also had some new features which\n"
"were very fancy, but some people thought,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:53.120--%3E00:47:56.123
msgid ""
"I don't want to rotate\n"
"my widgets on my desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:47:56.207--%3E00:48:00.378
msgid ""
"I'm not interested in the fancy new stuff.\n"
"One of the things that people complained"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:00.461--%3E00:48:05.466
msgid ""
"about a lot is we removed the ability\n"
"for you to put icons on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:05.549--%3E00:48:08.427
msgid ""
"Because, for example, for me,\n"
"I never see the desktop, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:08.511--%3E00:48:12.056
msgid ""
"But some of the people, like if you go\n"
"and watch my father's computer,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:12.139--%3E00:48:14.475
msgid "it's overflowing icons from the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:14.558--%3E00:48:16.894
msgid ""
"And we have ended up\n"
"adding it back, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:16.977--%3E00:48:21.232
msgid ""
"Because we realized we made a mistake\n"
"there. And there were fights."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:23.818--%3E00:48:27.696
msgid ""
"It was a pretty rough year\n"
"of feedback for the desktop team."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:27.780--%3E00:48:30.449
msgid "People were unhappy, and they let us know."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:31.242--%3E00:48:37.832
msgid ""
"I routinely get communication about how I\n"
"was, like, destroying KDE, and, you know,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:37.915--%3E00:48:41.710
msgid ""
"this was the end, and it was gonna die,\n"
"and it was all my fault."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:43.295--%3E00:48:47.299
msgid ""
"One group actually forked KDE 3\n"
"and maintained it as KDE Trinity,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:47.383--%3E00:48:52.304
msgid ""
"and they were very clear about why.\n"
"But there's also a lot of people"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:52.388--%3E00:48:56.684
msgid ""
"who saw what we were doing\n"
"and stuck with it and stuck with us."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:48:59.812--%3E00:49:04.275
msgid ""
"If we look back at the number of\n"
"contributors, that was actually growing,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:04.358--%3E00:49:09.613
msgid ""
"because it's not where I want it to be,\n"
"so I can complain or I can fix it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:09.697--%3E00:49:15.786
msgid ""
"And there was a lot of activity to fix the\n"
"problems. People started coming around,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:15.870--%3E00:49:20.249
msgid ""
"I think around 4.2, saying,\n"
"\"Yeah, it's getting somewhere."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:20.332--%3E00:49:22.084
msgid "I see where you guys are going.\""
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:22.168--%3E00:49:25.588
msgid ""
"And in the end, it took us, I think,\n"
"from start to finish, about five"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:25.671--%3E00:49:29.967
msgid ""
"and a half years before it was really good\n"
"and people started actually liking it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:30.050--%3E00:49:33.929
msgid ""
"And what's really nice is we're here\n"
"17 years after the initial development"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:34.013--%3E00:49:37.641
msgid ""
"of that started, I think.\n"
"It's evolved tremendously, and the people"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:37.725--%3E00:49:40.561
msgid ""
"who worked on it have done fantastic\n"
"things with it and continue to do,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:40.644--%3E00:49:43.647
msgid ""
"but it's still that same architecture.\n"
"The vision Aaron brought"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:43.731--%3E00:49:48.277
msgid ""
"in and his dedication and also\n"
"his ability to communicate this vision,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:48.360--%3E00:49:52.781
msgid ""
"I think this created a lot of energy\n"
"in KDE and brought projects forward."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:53.824--%3E00:49:59.079
msgid ""
"It was risky, but it's paid off.\n"
"Without KDE 4 and even the reaction to it,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:49:59.163--%3E00:50:03.709
msgid ""
"we would be a much less mature\n"
"community in the technology,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:03.792--%3E00:50:07.838
msgid ""
"but also as an organization,\n"
"as a community of people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:07.922--%3E00:50:12.051
msgid ""
"So all in all, it was not too bad.\n"
"It's just that, well,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:12.134--%3E00:50:16.555
msgid ""
"some of the users were a bit unhappy, but\n"
"we've won many of those over the years."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:16.639--%3E00:50:20.518
msgid ""
"There's people coming all the time saying,\n"
"oh, I used to be a KDE user,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:20.601--%3E00:50:24.313
msgid ""
"and then I left because it was not\n"
"so good during the KDE 4 time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:24.396--%3E00:50:26.232
msgid "And now I've tried it and it's amazing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:26.315--%3E00:50:30.819
msgid ""
"The best thing you can do is try\n"
"to do it better next time around."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:30.903--%3E00:50:35.991
msgid ""
"I'm pretty sure we did. And then if\n"
"you look at the Plasma 5 to 6 transition,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:36.075--%3E00:50:39.245
msgid "that was a very smooth upgrade."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:39.870--%3E00:50:43.832
msgid ""
"Two years ago, we got Plasma 6.\n"
"It's the latest Plasma."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 0 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:43.916--%3E00:50:44.792
msgid "It's very nice."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:44.875--%3E00:50:49.129
msgid ""
"It's very pretty. It has floating\n"
"taskbar at the bottom for some reason."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:50.798--%3E00:50:51.799
msgid "Today,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:52.299--%3E00:50:55.552
msgid ""
"KDE is better than ever.\n"
"It's a joy to work with."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:55.636--%3E00:50:57.221
msgid "I just bought a laptop last year,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:50:57.304--%3E00:51:00.307
msgid ""
"and it's the first time I've ever bought\n"
"a laptop with Linux pre-installed."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:00.391--%3E00:51:05.604
msgid ""
"And opening it up and seeing the glory of\n"
"Plasma Desktop on it was really rewarding."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:11.735--%3E00:51:17.491
msgid ""
"When web and cloud took over, people\n"
"asked themselves, does it matter anymore?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:17.574--%3E00:51:20.286
msgid ""
"If everything is running\n"
"within your browser,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:20.369--%3E00:51:22.871
msgid ""
"it doesn't matter what kind\n"
"of desktop environment you have."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:22.955--%3E00:51:24.915
msgid "You don't have local applications anymore."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:24.999--%3E00:51:28.085
msgid ""
"And that, of course,\n"
"led to the question, what is KDE?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:28.168--%3E00:51:30.337
msgid "KDE's original goal was: make a desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:30.421--%3E00:51:36.594
msgid ""
"Power on your computer and that UI you see\n"
"is KDE. We did this rebranding project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:36.677--%3E00:51:39.555
msgid ""
"One of the triggers for\n"
"that was the release of 4.0"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:39.638--%3E00:51:43.559
msgid "and people were saying okay KDE sucks."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:44.184--%3E00:51:45.728
msgid "Be that as it may,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 7 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:46.520--%3E00:51:53.819
msgid ""
"Plasma sucked, but there is a lot\n"
"of non-Plasma software that didn't."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:53.902--%3E00:51:59.283
msgid ""
"The community had grown so much, and they\n"
"had started writing application software,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:51:59.366--%3E00:52:01.952
msgid ""
"for example,\n"
"that was popular unto its own."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:02.036--%3E00:52:06.206
msgid ""
"The PDF viewer, you can use it in KDE,\n"
"you can use it in GNOME,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:06.290--%3E00:52:12.421
msgid ""
"you can use it in Windows.\n"
"So we needed to find a way that individual"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:12.504--%3E00:52:18.052
msgid ""
"groups within KDE could\n"
"basically screw up on their own."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:18.135--%3E00:52:22.598
msgid ""
"So these days, KDE is not\n"
"released as one blip of software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:22.681--%3E00:52:24.975
msgid ""
"The libraries are something,\n"
"the desktop is something,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:25.059--%3E00:52:27.394
msgid ""
"and our amazing applications\n"
"are their own thing as well."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:27.478--%3E00:52:31.565
msgid ""
"They deserve not to be tied to the\n"
"anchor of the desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:31.648--%3E00:52:35.778
msgid ""
"We started saying KDE is the community\n"
"rather than any particular product."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:35.861--%3E00:52:41.158
msgid ""
"We renamed the desktop product to Plasma.\n"
"And I think the migration to Git also had"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:41.241--%3E00:52:45.371
msgid ""
"a significant effect on how\n"
"the community structured itself,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:45.454--%3E00:52:49.666
msgid ""
"because then technically the projects\n"
"were not in the same repository anymore."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:49.750--%3E00:52:53.087
msgid ""
"And it made it easier to do releases,\n"
"allowed us to spread that work around,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:53.170--%3E00:52:54.797
msgid "but it also allowed us to rethink"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:54.880--%3E00:52:58.967
msgid ""
"and retool what it\n"
"was we were doing at its core."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:52:59.051--%3E00:53:03.472
msgid ""
"It was not at all clear what are\n"
"our shared values. Why are we doing that?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:03.555--%3E00:53:09.686
msgid ""
"How do we communicate it? It's hard\n"
"to agree that you have commitments unless"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:09.770--%3E00:53:14.066
msgid ""
"you in some way externalize them\n"
"and you put them down in writing."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:14.149--%3E00:53:18.404
msgid ""
"We ended up trying to come up\n"
"with a document that would cache all"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:18.487--%3E00:53:22.616
msgid ""
"of our widely held beliefs of what\n"
"it means to be part of KDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:22.700--%3E00:53:27.037
msgid ""
"Here we have the KDE manifesto\n"
"that we wrote back in 2012."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:27.121--%3E00:53:32.376
msgid ""
"And it starts, we are a community\n"
"of technologists, designers, writers"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:32.459--%3E00:53:37.965
msgid ""
"and advocates who work to ensure freedom\n"
"for all people through our software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:38.048--%3E00:53:41.677
msgid ""
"Because of this work,\n"
"we have come to value open governance,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:41.760--%3E00:53:46.932
msgid "free software, inclusivity, innovation,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:47.433--%3E00:53:52.688
msgid ""
"common ownership, end-user focus.\n"
"That is, in pursuit of our goal,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:52.771--%3E00:53:57.526
msgid ""
"we have found these items essential\n"
"to define and stay true to ourselves."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:57.609--%3E00:53:59.361
msgid "So we published that some years ago,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:53:59.445--%3E00:54:03.365
msgid ""
"and it was a distillation of everything\n"
"that we understood about the project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:03.449--%3E00:54:08.203
msgid ""
"It gives us a rudder in a storm, and it\n"
"ensures that as new people move in, yes,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:08.287--%3E00:54:10.581
msgid ""
"they will change the community\n"
"to reflect themselves as well,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:10.664--%3E00:54:15.127
msgid ""
"and that's a healthy thing. But the core\n"
"things that have made KDE successful over"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:15.210--%3E00:54:20.048
msgid ""
"these last 30 years maybe will be\n"
"maintained and continued forward."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:20.132--%3E00:54:25.012
msgid ""
"All these structures are\n"
"necessary in a project. Back then,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:25.095--%3E00:54:29.224
msgid ""
"we were more than 1,000 people worldwide\n"
"with different cultures communicating,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:29.308--%3E00:54:33.395
msgid "mostly online, and how it comes together,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:33.479--%3E00:54:37.983
msgid "how we form a community and make it work."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:38.066--%3E00:54:41.111
msgid "We started to do a lot of soul searching."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:41.195--%3E00:54:45.616
msgid ""
"You need to know who you are to tell\n"
"other people what you're out to do."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:46.116--%3E00:54:53.081
msgid ""
"This led to that we needed\n"
"to define a vision statement."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:53.165--%3E00:54:55.959
msgid "Many people expected it to be,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:54:56.043--%3E00:55:01.006
msgid ""
"we're making great software,\n"
"but our mission is about bringing freedom."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:03.675--%3E00:55:05.761
msgid "And one of the things"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:05.844--%3E00:55:10.682
msgid ""
"that is closely connected to freedom is\n"
"being able to be communicating in private,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:10.766--%3E00:55:16.897
msgid ""
"to be able to make your own choices.\n"
"And when I did a competitor analysis,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:16.980--%3E00:55:19.691
msgid ""
"many people thought it\n"
"would be the GNOME project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:19.775--%3E00:55:22.277
msgid ""
"If you look at our values,\n"
"they're aligning."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:22.361--%3E00:55:27.449
msgid ""
"We are definitely having\n"
"disagreements over how we get there."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:27.533--%3E00:55:33.497
msgid ""
"But fundamentally, they're our friends.\n"
"We need to kick Microsoft in the ass."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:33.580--%3E00:55:37.876
msgid ""
"We need to kick the big guys\n"
"that are stealing our freedom in the ass."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:37.960--%3E00:55:43.006
msgid ""
"Those are the guys we're after. Let's\n"
"not get us distracted from our friends."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:43.090--%3E00:55:45.759
msgid "This tribalism doesn't get us anywhere."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:45.842--%3E00:55:48.220
msgid ""
"The Linux desktop,\n"
"it's such a tiny market."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:48.303--%3E00:55:51.765
msgid ""
"I mean, it's not huge now,\n"
"but it was like exactly zero."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:51.848--%3E00:55:55.727
msgid ""
"And if we were fighting each other,\n"
"we would divide zero together."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:55:56.395--%3E00:56:00.440
msgid ""
"What we needed to do was find\n"
"ways to collaborate where we could"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:00.524--%3E00:56:04.152
msgid ""
"and cooperate as much as we could\n"
"bring ourselves to do so."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:04.236--%3E00:56:06.655
msgid "So we did the first desktop summit,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:06.738--%3E00:56:10.033
msgid ""
"which was the bringing together\n"
"of the two communities."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:10.117--%3E00:56:13.579
msgid ""
"There were people who were uncomfortable\n"
"with it, and that's part of it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:13.662--%3E00:56:16.707
msgid ""
"But overwhelmingly,\n"
"they had a great experience."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:16.790--%3E00:56:20.085
msgid ""
"Everybody walked away richer\n"
"than they had gone in."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:20.168--%3E00:56:24.298
msgid ""
"I'm working in a local school,\n"
"and we have a Linux room there,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:24.381--%3E00:56:26.758
msgid "which is now running with Debian 13,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:26.842--%3E00:56:31.179
msgid ""
"KDE-based, and another room\n"
"is now dual-boot with KDE."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:32.014--%3E00:56:34.975
msgid ""
"I mean, you are converting\n"
"the people to the project."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:35.058--%3E00:56:36.226
msgid "That's awesome."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:36.310--%3E00:56:41.231
msgid ""
"I'm trying to do something\n"
"which I think matters."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:41.315--%3E00:56:44.109
msgid ""
"Yeah, it does. Totally.\n"
"It was really cool to meet you, actually."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:44.192--%3E00:56:46.194
msgid ""
"I didn't catch your name.\n"
"Can you say the name again?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:46.278--%3E00:56:51.283
msgid ""
"Gerald. Gerald. Okay.\n"
"Gerald what? Senarclens de Grancy."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:51.366--%3E00:56:52.367
msgid "Very long."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:53.619--%3E00:56:58.874
msgid ""
"Yes. Joseph! It's difficult to say how\n"
"many users of KDE software there are"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:56:58.957--%3E00:57:04.796
msgid ""
"because we're nice and we don't spy on\n"
"our users. But we can say that there have"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:04.880--%3E00:57:09.176
msgid ""
"been a certain number of machines\n"
"with KDE software pre-installed on it."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:09.259--%3E00:57:13.847
msgid ""
"We also see it being used\n"
"very much in science and education."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:13.930--%3E00:57:17.768
msgid ""
"I know at one point the entire Brazilian\n"
"school system used KDE software"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:17.851--%3E00:57:20.520
msgid ""
"for primary schools.\n"
"This was 20 million machines."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:20.604--%3E00:57:25.567
msgid ""
"I know the entire public school system\n"
"of Valencia, Spain uses KDE software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:25.651--%3E00:57:29.446
msgid ""
"That's many machines. In the control\n"
"room of the Large Hadron Collider,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:29.529--%3E00:57:32.407
msgid ""
"probably the most complicated machine\n"
"that has ever been built."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:32.491--%3E00:57:36.036
msgid ""
"And if you head to the control room,\n"
"KDE is smiling at you from every screen."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:36.119--%3E00:57:38.413
msgid ""
"We know that the Steam Deck,\n"
"a commercial gaming console"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:38.497--%3E00:57:43.669
msgid ""
"that uses KDE Plasma as its desktop\n"
"environment, has sold millions of units."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:43.752--%3E00:57:47.089
msgid ""
"Each one of those units constitutes\n"
"a person using KDE software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:47.172--%3E00:57:49.966
msgid "It pops up in places you wouldn't expect."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:51.259--%3E00:57:53.845
msgid "archaeological expeditions, for example."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:53.929--%3E00:57:58.350
msgid ""
"Beyond that, it's difficult to say, but I\n"
"don't think it's a stretch to extrapolate"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:57:58.433--%3E00:58:01.019
msgid ""
"that there are millions\n"
"of users of KDE software,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:01.103--%3E00:58:05.482
msgid ""
"possibly tens of millions of users\n"
"out there. Using KDE software is easy."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:05.565--%3E00:58:10.737
msgid ""
"Installing an operating system\n"
"is something not everyone knows how to do,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:10.821--%3E00:58:14.074
msgid ""
"right? And it's not that Windows\n"
"is easier to install either,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:14.157--%3E00:58:16.201
msgid ""
"it's just that people\n"
"buy it pre-installed."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:16.284--%3E00:58:19.996
msgid ""
"As we know, the way normal people get\n"
"software is they use it on whatever device"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:20.080--%3E00:58:23.208
msgid ""
"they already purchased, right?\n"
"Normal people don't buy a device,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:23.291--%3E00:58:25.794
msgid ""
"erase the operating system,\n"
"and put a whole new one on there."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:25.877--%3E00:58:27.379
msgid "This is what's very scary."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:27.462--%3E00:58:31.633
msgid ""
"And I think as long as this is the way\n"
"to get an operating system with KDE Plasma"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:31.717--%3E00:58:35.929
msgid ""
"on it, we're going to struggle\n"
"to hit 10% market share."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:36.722--%3E00:58:41.143
msgid ""
"But if we can partner with hardware\n"
"vendors who are tired of Windows"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:41.226--%3E00:58:45.564
msgid ""
"and tired of macOS and tired\n"
"of other things, And we can say, hey,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:45.647--%3E00:58:49.735
msgid ""
"we have an alternative for you. It's\n"
"ready to go. It runs on your hardware."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:49.818--%3E00:58:52.779
msgid "It's QA'd. We can work with you."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:52.863--%3E00:58:56.241
msgid ""
"Eventually, these hardware companies are\n"
"going to start to think, well, shoot,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:56.324--%3E00:58:59.578
msgid ""
"why shouldn't I do that? And that's\n"
"the point at which it snowballs."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:58:59.661--%3E00:59:02.372
msgid ""
"And I think you'll see market\n"
"share of Linux in general"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:02.456--%3E00:59:05.792
msgid ""
"and KDE specifically not\n"
"going from 1% to 2% to 3%,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:05.876--%3E00:59:12.132
msgid ""
"but going from 10% to 20% to 30% to 40%\n"
"very quickly. And I think this is coming."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:12.215--%3E00:59:15.886
msgid ""
"I think this is coming because the world\n"
"is getting tired of proprietary software"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:15.969--%3E00:59:18.472
msgid "and proprietary operating systems."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:18.555--%3E00:59:22.058
msgid ""
"There's only so long you can abuse\n"
"people before they say, you know what,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:22.142--%3E00:59:25.854
msgid ""
"I've got freedom. I can just stop.\n"
"I can use something else."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:25.937--%3E00:59:27.606
msgid "And when they make that decision,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:27.689--%3E00:59:34.070
msgid ""
"I want them to come to us because\n"
"we are empowered by humane values."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:34.154--%3E00:59:35.489
msgid "We focus on people."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:46.625--%3E00:59:51.922
msgid ""
"If somebody had asked me in fall '96,\n"
"will this still be around in 30 years?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:52.005--%3E00:59:53.256
msgid "I don't know, I probably would have said,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:53.340--%3E00:59:56.635
msgid ""
"I don't know if I'm still going\n"
"to be around 30 years, who knows?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:56.718--%3E00:59:59.137
msgid ""
"Yeah, I mean, we have been doing\n"
"this thing for a long time."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 00:59:59.221--%3E01:00:02.349
msgid ""
"And it's one of those things\n"
"that maybe shouldn't have worked."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:02.432--%3E01:00:06.311
msgid ""
"I think it's marvelous that so many\n"
"people can collaborate on something"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:06.394--%3E01:00:09.856
msgid "so complicated and it doesn't fall apart."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:09.940--%3E01:00:14.110
msgid ""
"KDE always has been first\n"
"a source of innovation."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 6 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:14.194--%3E01:00:20.992
msgid ""
"We know in KDE that the repository\n"
"is being checked out daily from Microsoft."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:21.076--%3E01:00:24.496
msgid ""
"And once in a while I see a new\n"
"feature in Windows and I think,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:24.579--%3E01:00:26.248
msgid "hey, I know this feature."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:26.331--%3E01:00:30.836
msgid ""
"We see constant growth, which is special\n"
"over such a long period of time,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:30.919--%3E01:00:32.295
msgid "even just staying relevant."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:32.379--%3E01:00:36.007
msgid ""
"I think it's actually more\n"
"relevant than it ever has been."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 5 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:36.091--%3E01:00:41.346
msgid ""
"Certain things that inform the computing\n"
"landscape today were not actually big"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:41.429--%3E01:00:45.016
msgid ""
"factors when we started.\n"
"Internet was still ramping up."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:45.100--%3E01:00:48.019
msgid ""
"You didn't really have\n"
"software as a service yet."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:48.103--%3E01:00:51.481
msgid ""
"You didn't have subscription-based\n"
"software business models."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:51.565--%3E01:00:54.568
msgid ""
"The need for security,\n"
"the need for privacy,"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:54.651--%3E01:00:59.281
msgid ""
"the need for control and resilience\n"
"will increase in the future."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:00:59.364--%3E01:01:02.367
msgid ""
"So the desktop will have a renaissance,\n"
"I'm pretty sure about that."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:02.450--%3E01:01:06.621
msgid ""
"I think a lot of times proprietary\n"
"software is like the metaphorical frog"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:06.705--%3E01:01:08.540
msgid "in the boiling pot of water, right?"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:08.623--%3E01:01:13.545
msgid ""
"You don't notice what you're losing as\n"
"it's happening until it's almost too late."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:13.628--%3E01:01:18.466
msgid ""
"And my hope is that when people do make\n"
"that realization, KDE is there for them."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:18.550--%3E01:01:23.221
msgid ""
"And we can save people from being in that\n"
"pot of boiling water in the first place."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:23.305--%3E01:01:27.517
msgid ""
"The world needs an open\n"
"option for the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 4 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:27.601--%3E01:01:32.063
msgid ""
"This is so important in a world where\n"
"everything we do is based on software."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 3 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:33.648--%3E01:01:37.402
msgid ""
"And so KDE has a really\n"
"important flame to keep lit."
msgstr ""

#. visible for 1 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:37.485--%3E01:01:39.196
msgid "It's the world's backstop to making sure"
msgstr ""

#. visible for 2 seconds
#. +> trunk5
#: 01:01:39.279--%3E01:01:42.157
msgid ""
"that we don't leave whole\n"
"groups of people behind."
msgstr ""
